# An error in library code is always reported, with the note that says whose code it
# is. The warning beside it in the same template is the author's: the author's build
# reports it, because a template is checked where it is written (#1070), and the
# consumer does not (#1007). A template fault is the author's too, so the error here is
# one that only an instance has: the template uses `a` two times, which copies an `i32`
# and moves a `string`, so the `string` instance in the consumer's build is the fault.
# BUILD_LIB_WARNS: lint_err_lib.sushi -> CW1001
# EXPECT_ERROR_CODES_EXACT: CE2405
# EXPECT_STDERR_CONTAINS: is a source library, compiled here because of `use <lib/lint_err_lib>`
use <lib/lint_err_lib>

fn main() i32:
    println(widen(nom "text".clone()))
    return 0
